{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779420-isn-t-the-dragonfire-atavism-a-bit-strange-for-beasts-nicknamed-as-lurkers","id":779420,"title":"Isn't The Dragonfire Atavism A Bit Strange For Beasts Nicknamed As Lurkers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-03T18:31:26-08:00","id":779420,"title":"Isn't The Dragonfire Atavism A Bit Strange For Beasts Nicknamed As Lurkers?","content":"Limb From Limb, Relentless Hunter and From The Shadows all sound thematically fitting, but breathing fire is really flashy. Since fire can bring down havens and force people to drop their scalding weapons and armor, it's a great way to remove protections and thus more fitting for the Ugallu. Furthermore, Raptor is closer to a dragon than Lurker. As a result, Needs Must would become an Eshmaki Atavism, as it fits more closely with the idea of a monster that can always find you, but is never seen for more than a terrifying split second.<br /> <br /> Does this sound reasonable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-03-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:40:28-08:00","id":779430,"title":"","content":"Eshmaki are nightmares of doom from the dark, of the oblivion waiting where you can't see, and of unexpected and demoralizing destruction. Dragonfire seems just fine for them. Needs Must is much closer to the Ugallu as nightmares of exposure, of claustrophobia, of paranoia and unseen observation, and doesn't really fall within the Eshmaki purview by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T18:58:29-08:00","id":779444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779420-isn-t-the-dragonfire-atavism-a-bit-strange-for-beasts-nicknamed-as-lurkers?p=779430#post779430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eshmaki are nightmares of doom from the dark, of the oblivion waiting where you can't see, and of unexpected and demoralizing destruction. Dragonfire seems just fine for them. Needs Must is much closer to the Ugallu as nightmares of exposure, of claustrophobia, of paranoia and unseen observation, and doesn't really fall within the Eshmaki purview by comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're right. Come to think of it, I'm just bothered by the &quot;dragon&quot; part of the Atavism. I associate Dragonfire with Wings Of The Raptor, because of the classic image of dragons breathing fire while flying. IIRC, you can re-fluff Atavisms to make them more fitting for different Horrors, such as saying your Namtaru's &quot;Dragonfire&quot; is actually a stream of sticky, corrosive vomit. All Atavisms are open to all Beasts, so it's just a nitpick. But what could I rename Dragonfire as, then? How about Ruinous Breath or Breath Of Devastation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-03-2015, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:27:11-08:00","id":779476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779420-isn-t-the-dragonfire-atavism-a-bit-strange-for-beasts-nicknamed-as-lurkers?p=779444#post779444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're right. Come to think of it, I'm just bothered by the &quot;dragon&quot; part of the Atavism. I associate Dragonfire with Wings Of The Raptor, because of the classic image of dragons breathing fire while flying. IIRC, you can re-fluff Atavisms to make them more fitting for different Horrors, such as saying your Namtaru's &quot;Dragonfire&quot; is actually a stream of sticky, corrosive vomit. All Atavisms are open to all Beasts, so it's just a nitpick. But what could I rename Dragonfire as, then? How about Ruinous Breath or Breath Of Devastation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It makes me wonder how the Dragonfire Atavism could be reworked for, say, a Makara. Would it be acid like the Namtaru? Or does lightning seem more appropriate, especially if the Horror in question is similar to a jellyfish, manta ray, or eel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T19:44:45-08:00","id":779489,"title":"","content":"It reminded me of an animated movie I watch (many, many times) as a kid; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Flight_of_Dragons\" target=\"_blank\">The Flight of Dragons</a>. My favourite scene is where the protagonist reinterprets the 'magical' abilities of dragons in more modern terminology. Including how dragons breath fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T05:11:33-08:00","id":779715,"title":"","content":"All but two of the Atavisms are &quot;dragon-y&quot; in some way (Infestation, Siren's Treacherous Song). You want other elements, we have Atavisms that cover those powers already. Actually, we have atavisms for all four main elements - fire (Dragonfire), wind/lightning (Storm Lash), water (Heart of Ocean), earth (Titanic Blow for tremor shocks) and poison for a fifth (Basilisk Touch is a better acid twist than dragonfire). And that's before call down the Lair. When we combine both Lair and the above Atavisms, we get a rather well rounded elemental power set.<br /> <br /> As for why Dragonfire is affinity for the Eshmaki? The Eshmaki are as much all about bright light as well as shadows - why else would Blazing Light be a suggested Lair trait along with Poor Light and Darkness? Light and dark are both aspects that the Eshmaki delight in, and fire is very much tied into that bright light aspects of the family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-04-2015, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T05:33:18-08:00","id":779725,"title":"","content":"Both Blinding Light and Obscuring Darkness can hide things, A Dragon might swoop down and snatch you up or it could hide in the Darkness/Volcano mouth and wait for you to notice it. That rock your seeing with the lava falling off of it? Yeah that's not a rock....<br /> And let's be honest... Sometimes the thing that scares us is the thing that stands in the light.. watching you waiting for you to notice it. (Incidentially.. Anyone else think It Follows could be a good inspiration for a Eshmaki Predator/Nemesis?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}